From: limina <gustavo@noronha.eti.br>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: stop free-page reporting across suspend/resume

virtballoon_freeze() calls remove_common() -- which resets the device and
frees the virtqueues via del_vqs() -- on the assumption, stated in its
comment, that "the workqueue is already frozen by the PM core". That is
true of the balloon's own freezable workqueue, but free-page reporting is
driven from page_reporting_process() on the system ("events") workqueue,
which is NOT freezable. So a page-reporting run can execute during
suspend-to-idle after the reporting virtqueue has been freed and
use-after-free it, oopsing in virtqueue_add_inbuf()
(Workqueue: events page_reporting_process -> virtballoon_free_page_report).
With the default console_suspend=Y the resulting mid-suspend oops then
wedges the subsequent resume inside dpm_resume(), hanging the guest.

virtballoon_remove() already handles this correctly by calling
page_reporting_unregister() (which cancels the reporting work
synchronously) before remove_common(). Mirror that in the freeze path, and
re-register page reporting in virtballoon_restore() after the virtqueues
are back.

Reproduced on aarch64 under libkrun/Hypervisor.framework (limina) with a
guest that negotiates VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_REPORTING: `rtcwake -m freeze`
oopses ~1.5s into s2idle and never resumes; removing virtio_balloon or
applying this patch makes the cycle pass repeatably.

Signed-off-by: limina <gustavo@noronha.eti.br>
---
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c	2026-07-18 13:21:15
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c	2026-07-18 13:21:27
@@ -1128,9 +1128,18 @@
 	struct virtio_balloon *vb = vdev->priv;
 
 	/*
-	 * The workqueue is already frozen by the PM core before this
-	 * function is called.
+	 * The balloon's own workqueue is frozen by the PM core, but free-page
+	 * reporting runs on the system (events) workqueue, which is not
+	 * freezable. remove_common() below resets the device and frees the
+	 * virtqueues, so a page-reporting run racing suspend-to-idle would
+	 * use-after-free the (now dead) reporting vq and oops in
+	 * virtqueue_add_inbuf(). Unregister page reporting first -- it cancels
+	 * its work synchronously -- mirroring virtballoon_remove();
+	 * virtballoon_restore() re-registers it.
 	 */
+	if (virtio_has_feature(vb->vdev, VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_REPORTING))
+		page_reporting_unregister(&vb->pr_dev_info);
+
 	remove_common(vb);
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1146,6 +1155,12 @@
 
 	virtio_device_ready(vdev);
 
+	if (virtio_has_feature(vdev, VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_REPORTING)) {
+		ret = page_reporting_register(&vb->pr_dev_info);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	if (towards_target(vb))
 		virtballoon_changed(vdev);
 	update_balloon_size(vb);
